  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1225 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nA weak cold front is expected to be over the Big Country early\nSaturday morning and will push south across the remainder of the \nforecast area during the day. A few showers and thunderstorms \nwill be possible along and ahead of the front into early Saturday\nevening but rain chances will remain rather low (20 to 30%).\nTemperatures will be a little cooler as well, with highs Saturday\nafternoon in the mid to upper 90s. Sunday will be dry, with highs\na degree or two warmer than Saturday. \n\nAs we head into next week, the upper high will be centered over\nthe Four Corners region, with the ridge axis extending into \nTexas. This will result in a continuation of dry and hot weather \nthrough late week, with highs back in the upper 90s to low 100s.",
